CON-01: give a closed storage unit no free surface above its full depth

A storage unit with a surcharge depth is closed: storage_getVolume() caps its
volume at fullVolume above full depth. But initNodeStates() still gave it its
curve area there, so whenever setNodeDepth() integrates the depth by area
above full depth (always under SURCHARGE_METHOD SLOT; under EXTRAN when no
link responds to head) the depth rose and fell through the surcharge band as
if it held A*SurDepth of water that the volume never books. Set the node's
own area to 0 above full depth, so in the band it behaves like a junction in
surcharge (its links' areas, floored at MinSurfArea). EXTRAN storage units
with conduits use the dQ/dH branch there and are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-01_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c b/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
index 972da8c..6a62be5 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
@@ -311,6 +311,11 @@ void initNodeStates()
             Xnode[i].newSurfArea = node_getSurfArea(i, Node[i].newDepth);
         }
 
+        // --- a closed storage unit has no free surface above its full depth
+        if ( Node[i].type == STORAGE && Node[i].surDepth > 0.0 &&
+             Node[i].newDepth > Node[i].fullDepth )
+            Xnode[i].newSurfArea = 0.0;
+
         // --- initialize nodal inflow & outflow
         Node[i].inflow = 0.0;
         Node[i].outflow = Node[i].losses;
